  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "5Zfo7/59XNCGIl8k8o5DNWLF9iE=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The buttons inside `DocumentToolbar` accept `ToolbarButtonProps`:\n\n```ts\n{\n  document?: PHDocument;\n  children?: ReactNode;\n  className?: string;\n  onClick?: (document?: PHDocument) => void;\n}\n```\n\n`className` is merged into the button's defaults via `twMerge`, `children` replaces the default button contents, and `onClick` replaces the default behavior. Their default styling is:\n\n- **Undo/Redo/Download/Switchboard/History/Close**: the shared `ToolbarButton` base \u2014 `grid size-fit place-items-center rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-1 text-foreground` plus hover/active/disabled effects\n- **Download button**: same base, with a `<span className=\"px-1 text-xs\">Download</span>` label instead of an icon\n- **Document name**: `<h1>` with `text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground` (`ToolbarName` takes `titleClassName` / `inputClassName`)\n\nEvery button is exported individually (`ToolbarButton`, `ToolbarUndoButton`, `ToolbarRedoButton`, `ToolbarDownloadButton`, `ToolbarSwitchboardButton`, `ToolbarHistoryButton`, `ToolbarCloseButton`, `ToolbarName`), so the way to customize one is to wrap it and pass it back through `componentOverrides`:\n\n```tsx\n<DocumentToolbar\n  document={document}\n  componentOverrides={{\n    download: (props) => (\n      <ToolbarDownloadButton\n        {...props}\n        className=\"!bg-[#1e1e2e] !border-white/10\"\n      >\n        <span>Export</span>\n      </ToolbarDownloadButton>\n    ),\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nOr render the buttons yourself inside `children` for complete control over the toolbar contents.\n\nTailwind arbitrary child selectors (`[&_button]`, `[&_button_svg]`, `[&_h1]`, ...) passed through `toolbarClassName` still work as a blanket theming shortcut, but they are no longer required \u2014 they were a workaround for buttons that did not expose style props, and the buttons now do.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:45.000Z"
    }
  },
